A text can be drawn at the size it was given whatever the person's text size,
for lettering that stands in for a picture on a tile of a fixed width: scaled
with the system's text size, a word wider than the tile is broken across two
lines. `fixed-size` on a text says so, and both renderers draw it at the size
it names; everything else still scales.

